{#- Article 03: a mailbox key sits on the ring of node identifiers; its 5
    closest nodes (XOR distance, drawn here as nearness on the ring) are its
    responsibles. Conversation mailboxes change every day, so the key and the
    responsibles move. No message path here, so no transport colour: the
    responsibles are filled accent dots, the others hollow. Coordinates come
    from a small generator script. No blank line (Markdown). -#}
{%- set t = {
  en: {
    title: "A mailbox lives on the five closest relays, and moves every day",
    desc: "Two rings of node identifiers, the same network on two days. On day N the mailbox key falls in one place and the five nodes closest to it are its responsibles. On day N+1 the conversation uses a new mailbox, its key falls elsewhere, and five other nodes are responsible.",
    key: "mailbox key", resp: "responsibles", ids: "node IDs", dayN: "day N", dayN1: "day N+1"
  },
  fr: {
    title: "Une boîte vit sur les cinq relais les plus proches et change chaque jour",
    desc: "Deux anneaux d’identifiants de nœuds, le même réseau deux jours de suite. Le jour N, la clé de la boîte tombe à un endroit et les cinq nœuds les plus proches en sont les responsables. Le jour N+1, la conversation utilise une nouvelle boîte, sa clé tombe ailleurs et cinq autres nœuds en sont responsables.",
    key: "clé de la boîte", resp: "responsables", ids: "identifiants", dayN: "jour N", dayN1: "jour N+1"
  }
}[lang] -%}
<svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 720 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="mailbox-placement-title mailbox-placement-desc" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="13">
<title id="mailbox-placement-title">{{ t.title }}</title>
<desc id="mailbox-placement-desc">{{ t.desc }}</desc>
